        "obligationId": "scenario%3Afile-owner-without-destination-write-grant::entry%3Apost-process-file",
        "conclusion": "source_supported_failure",
        "explanation": "At the declared entry, process_file authenticates the caller with get_verified_user and, for a non-admin, retrieves the file through get_file_by_id_and_user_id using the caller's user ID. This validates/binds access to the source file, not permission to write to the selected destination collection. The caller-supplied collection_name is accepted and passed to save_docs_to_vector_db with add=True. That helper recognizes an existing collection and, because add is true, does not return early; it ultimately calls VECTOR_DB_CLIENT.insert with the selected collection name and generated items. No destination ownership or explicit destination write-grant check is invoked on this path. The separately defined _validate_collection_access helper supports an access_type parameter but is not called by process_file in the supplied path. Therefore, under the stated premises and accepted policy, the source-visible behavior is that the user can reach the destination write sink; the source does not enforce the required destination authorization before the sink.",
        "facts": {
          "entry": [
            {
              "statement": "POST /process/file dispatches to process_file, which receives the verified user dependency.",
              "citations": [
                {
                  "path": "backend/open_webui/routers/retrieval.py",
                  "startLine": 1546,
                  "endLine": 1552,
                  "quote": "@router.post('/process/file')\nasync def process_file(\n    request: Request,\n    form_data: ProcessFileForm,\n    user=Depends(get_verified_user),\n    db: AsyncSession = Depends(get_async_session),\n):"
                }
              ]
            }
          ],
          "binding": [
            {
              "statement": "process_file uses the caller-supplied collection_name, defaulting only when it is absent, and passes that value as collection_name to the vector-save helper.",
              "citations": [
                {
                  "path": "backend/open_webui/routers/retrieval.py",
                  "startLine": 1564,
                  "endLine": 1571,
                  "quote": "    if file:\n        try:\n            collection_name = form_data.collection_name\n\n            if collection_name is None:\n                collection_name = f'file-{file.id}'\n\n            if form_data.content:"
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "statement": "For a non-admin caller, process_file retrieves the file using the supplied file ID together with user.id.",
              "citations": [
                {
                  "path": "backend/open_webui/routers/retrieval.py",
                  "startLine": 1559,
                  "endLine": 1564,
                  "quote": "    if user.role == 'admin':\n        file = await Files.get_file_by_id(form_data.file_id, db=db)\n    else:\n        file = await Files.get_file_by_id_and_user_id(form_data.file_id, user.id, db=db)\n\n    if file:"
                }
              ]
            }
          ],
          "control": [
            {
              "statement": "The supplied source separately defines _validate_collection_access, which filters requested collections and can reject denied access, but the shown process_file path does not invoke it.",
              "citations": [
                {
                  "path": "backend/open_webui/routers/retrieval.py",
                  "startLine": 2339,
                  "endLine": 2352,
                  "quote": "async def _validate_collection_access(collection_names: list[str], user, access_type: str = 'read') -> None:\n    \"\"\"\n    Raise 403 if the user lacks access to any of the requested collections.\n    Delegates to the shared filter_accessible_collections utility so the\n    access rules stay in one place.\n    \"\"\"\n    requested = set(collection_names)\n    allowed = await filter_accessible_collections(requested, user, access_type=access_type)\n    denied = requested - allowed\n    if denied:\n        raise HTTPException(\n            status_code=status.HTTP_403_FORBIDDEN,\n            detail=ERROR_MESSAGES.ACCESS_PROHIBITED,\n        )"
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "statement": "The visible authorization control checks the non-admin caller's ownership/access to the source file through get_file_by_id_and_user_id; no destination collection ownership or write-grant check appears before the save call.",
              "citations": [
                {
                  "path": "backend/open_webui/routers/retrieval.py",
                  "startLine": 1559,
                  "endLine": 1564,
                  "quote": "    if user.role == 'admin':\n        file = await Files.get_file_by_id(form_data.file_id, db=db)\n    else:\n        file = await Files.get_file_by_id_and_user_id(form_data.file_id, user.id, db=db)\n\n    if file:"
                }
              ]
            }
          ],
          "effect": [
            {
              "statement": "save_docs_to_vector_db inserts the generated text/vector items into the selected collection through VECTOR_DB_CLIENT.insert.",
              "citations": [
                {
                  "path": "backend/open_webui/routers/retrieval.py",
                  "startLine": 1517,
                  "endLine": 1531,
                  "quote": "        items = [\n            {\n                'id': str(uuid.uuid4()),\n                'text': text,\n                'vector': embeddings[idx],\n                'metadata': metadatas[idx],\n            }\n            for idx, text in enumerate(texts)\n        ]\n\n        log.info(f'adding to collection {collection_name}')\n        VECTOR_DB_CLIENT.insert(\n            collection_name=collection_name,\n            items=items,\n        )"
                }
              ]
            }
          ],
          "condition": [
            {
              "statement": "save_docs_to_vector_db detects an existing collection and proceeds when add is true; it returns early only when both overwrite is false and add is false.",
              "citations": [
                {
                  "path": "backend/open_webui/routers/retrieval.py",
                  "startLine": 1458,
                  "endLine": 1467,
                  "quote": "    try:\n        if VECTOR_DB_CLIENT.has_collection(collection_name=collection_name):\n            log.info(f'collection {collection_name} already exists')\n\n            if overwrite:\n                VECTOR_DB_CLIENT.delete_collection(collection_name=collection_name)\n                log.info(f'deleting existing collection {collection_name}')\n            elif add is False:\n                log.info(f'collection {collection_name} already exists, overwrite is False and add is False')\n                return True"
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "statement": "When embedding and retrieval are not bypassed, process_file invokes save_docs_to_vector_db with the selected collection_name and sets add to true when collection_name was supplied by the caller.",
              "citations": [
                {
                  "path": "backend/open_webui/routers/retrieval.py",
                  "startLine": 1683,
                  "endLine": 1705,
                  "quote": "                try:\n                    # Commit any pending changes before the slow embedding step.\n                    # Note: file is already a Pydantic model (not ORM), so no expunge needed.\n                    await db.commit()\n\n                    # External embedding API takes time (5-60s+).\n                    # Subsequent updates use fresh async sessions.\n                    # NOTE: save_docs_to_vector_db is a sync function that\n                    # calls asyncio.run_coroutine_threadsafe(..., main_loop).result()\n                    # which blocks the calling thread.  We MUST run it in a\n                    # worker thread to avoid deadlocking the event loop.\n                    result = await run_in_threadpool(\n                        save_docs_to_vector_db,\n                        request,\n                        docs=docs,\n                        collection_name=collection_name,\n                        metadata={\n                            'file_id': file.id,\n                            'name': file.filename,\n                            'hash': hash,\n                        },\n                        add=(True if form_data.collection_name else False),\n                        user=user,"
                }
              ]
